Chapter: SessionTypes

 Session types for protocol-safe channels. A session protocol is a
 sequence of send and receive steps encoded as nested phantom types.
 The channel type SChan s carries the current protocol state s; each
 operation (s-send, s-recv, s-close) consumes the channel and returns
 a new one at the next state. The type checker verifies the protocol
 is followed in order.

 Protocol definition example:

   MyProto = SSend Integer (SRecv Text SEnd)

 This says: send an Integer, then receive a Text, then close.
 The dual (server side) is: SRecv Integer (SSend Text SEnd).

 We say:

Section: Protocol State Types

  SSend a s = | MkSSend
  SRecv a s = | MkSRecv
  SEnd = | MkSEnd

  SChan s = | MkSChan (Integer)

Section: Dual

  SDual s = | MkSDual

